course: dictionary
lesson: 9051
title: A sleepover, in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sleepover is a party or visit when a child stays the night at a friend's house. The words around it give clues: games, films and snacks. «At a sleepover Lily tells Maddie she has a crush on Kieran.» Even without a dictionary, you can tell that a sleepover is a place where friends talk and share secrets.
explain: Sleepovers come with good manners. Say thank you to the host's parents, follow their house rules and help tidy up. «At a sleepover in Kent, Leo-Ray burns the toast because at home staff always made it, and everyone laughs; he laughs too, then asks his friend's mum to show him.» Laughing at a mistake and asking for help is good manners.
explain: Your parents should always know where you are. You can call home if you feel uncomfortable, and it is fine to say no to a sleepover. «In Bradford, Tariq's dad, strict and religious and warm underneath, says no to a sleepover party, then drives Tariq there and picks him up at nine.» A parent's no is a decision you can respect, even if you are disappointed.
explain: Sleepovers can also be taken away as a consequence. «Meanwhile Jake's mum bans sleepovers for a month because he was rude to his teacher.» The word bans means stops something on purpose, so the sleepovers are paused for a whole month.
fact: A sleepover is a party or visit when a child stays the night at a friend's house.
fact: Sleepovers often include games, films and snacks.
fact: Useful phrases: have a sleepover, go to a sleepover, sleepover party.
fact: The plural of sleepover is sleepovers.
fact: No adult or older child should ask you to keep secrets or break rules, and you can always tell a trusted adult.
exercise: What is a sleepover? | *A party or visit when a child stays the night at a friend's house | A school trip to a museum | A quick run before breakfast | A family meal in a restaurant
exercise: Which three things are often part of a sleepover? | Football, swimming and shopping | Homework, tests and spelling lists | Trains, buses and taxis | *Games, films and snacks
exercise: «Leo-Ray burns the toast and laughs, then asks his friend's mum to show him.» What good manner does this show? | Shouting at the host | Refusing to eat anything at all | *Laughing at a mistake and asking for help | Hiding in his room all night
test: What should you do at a sleepover to show good manners? | Ignore the house rules | *Say thank you to the host's parents and help tidy up | Keep a secret from your parents | Leave the mess for the host to clear
test: «Tariq's dad says no to a sleepover party.» Which statement is true? | *It is fine to say no to a sleepover, and parents can make that choice | You must always go to every sleepover you are invited to | Saying no is always rude | Only adults are allowed to say no
exam: Which is the plural of sleepover? | *sleepovers | sleepovering | sleepoverses | sleepover's
